{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_016GeL6pYK2TEeDe1QVdbsSB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was completed:\n\n**Written:** `ai-engineering/answers/04-004-what-is-rlhf-and-why-important.md`\n\nKey content:\n- **Concept:** Why SFT alone is insufficient for alignment — it imitates good outputs but can't optimize relative preferences between responses\n- **Mechanism:** Full 3-stage pipeline — SFT → reward model (pairwise ranking loss: `L = -log σ(r_chosen - r_rejected)`) → PPO with KL penalty (`β · KL(π_RL || π_SFT)`) to prevent reward hacking\n- **Example:** InstructGPT — 1.3B RLHF model rated better than 175B GPT-3 base by humans 85% of the time; 33K pairwise comparisons used\n- **RLHF vs DPO table:** DPO eliminates the RM and PPO via closed-form derivation; now the default for most practitioners (Llama 2, Mistral Instruct)\n- **Pitfalls:** Not knowing the KL leash, not mentioning DPO, conflating alignment with capability improvement\n\n**9 items remaining** in the Next queue (Q5–Q12 + validate)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":327,"cache_read_input_tokens":67846,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":327,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6df79f3d-a3a9-4006-bb5c-d94ba7d74435","uuid":"2be0ffa5-1a4f-490c-921f-3f7849f0daa1"}
